# PowerPoint files (master deck, generated proposals, test output)
*.pptx

# Source brochure PDF
*.pdf

# Rendered slide images and the decks they came from (tests/render_scenarios.py).
# Build artefacts, and large.
tests/_rendered/
tests/_render_smoke/

# Wide Orbit exports dropped in the project root for reference.
*.xlsx
*.xls

# Reports generated from the real audience usage workbook -- real segment
# names and real delivered-impression volumes, same reason the workbook
# itself is gitignored. audience_component_overrides.csv is NOT here --
# it's the permanent, committed decisions registry (component/action/
# category only, no impressions), the same kind of real-segment-name data
# audience_segments_derived.csv has always carried in this repo.
audience_usage_uncategorized.txt
clt_excluded_segments.txt
audience_uncategorized_markup.csv

# Wide Orbit test fixtures. These are REAL client schedules -- real advertisers,
# real rates, real costs -- so they're held out of the repo pending a decision
# about whether that belongs on GitHub. tests/test_wideorbit.py reports SKIP
# when they're absent rather than failing, so the suite still runs without them.
tests/fixtures/wideorbit/

# Raw live-model responses saved by tests/test_draft_live.py --save. They're
# a diagnostic for one run, not a fixture -- the committed .draft.json files
# are what Tier 1 replays.
tests/fixtures/*.live.json

# Case study source decks -- the vault's contents live in Supabase storage,
# not the repo. (*.pptx already covers the decks; this catches the stray
# shortcut/metadata files that come along with a OneDrive export.)
case_studies_source/

